locked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Configuration\n\n```toml\n[leveldb2]\nenabled = false\n\n[redis_cluster2]\nenabled = true\naddresses = [\"redis-cluster:6379\"]\nusername = \"seaweedfs\"\npassword = \"pass\"\n# prefix for filer redis keys\nkeyPrefix = \"seaweedfs\"\n```\n\nOn Redis I have configured an ACL so the `seaweedfs` user can only access keys prefixed with `seaweedfs`, i.e:\n```\n user seaweedfs on >pass ~*:seaweedfs:* -@all +@keyspace +@connection +@read +@write +cluster|slots\n```\nWhen filer starts I get the following error:\n\n```\n11:25:21.640235 filer.go:187 read filer.store.id= : NOPERM No permissions to access a key\n```\n\nThis happens when reading the `filer.store.id` from redis:\nhttps://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/blob/77dcb20a7485074d37340985d53103f94538abe6/weed/filer/filer.go#L173\n\nRedis KvGet doesn't seem to respect `KeyPrefix`\nhttps://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/blob/69553e5ba6d46ed924b0c3adc3f8d9666550999a/weed/filer/redis2/universal_redis_store_kv.go#L22-L31\n\nRemoving the prefix restriction from redis ACL causes seaweedfs to create the key without the prefix defined in the configuration.","closed_by":{"login":"chrislusf","id":1543151,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NDMxNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1543151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf","html_url":"https://github.com/chrislusf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/events{/privacy}","received_event